57bm-i1c"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i1c"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i1c","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.91 (The signed endpoint recurrence)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.91, p. 70, label record:257bm-i1c","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*The signed next-step expression is $H(D,k,n)=2S(D,k,n-1)+1-c_D(n)$. The last term counts the selected exponents dividing the new endpoint. This is the same recurrence shape as the generic tempered-orbit recurrence $u(N+1)=2u(N)-v\\cdot c(N+1)$ from the tempered-orbit criterion (Theorem 6.105 below), specialised to Mersenne local repair. A matching recurrence alone does not imply rationality: Theorem 6.105 also requires one fixed coefficient sequence, integer states and a vanishing scaled limit. Those additional conditions must be checked before that criterion can be applied to these finite-row quantities.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1c","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i1c","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1c%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_endpoint_term_counts_divisors%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i1c%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_endpoint_term_counts_divisors%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_endpoint_term_counts_divisors"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0